ID BAR MICRON
SOL 103
CEND
TITLE = 103_bar_micron: 1 UM CANTILEVER, 10 CBARS, SI UNITS (KG-M-S)
SUBTI = ELEMENT MASSES ~5E-18 KG, BELOW THE OLD ABSOLUTE EPSIL(1) MASS FILTER
$
$ Regression test for unit-independent mass filtering (MASS_MATRIX_ASSEMBLY).
$ Every mass term (4.66E-18 kg per grid, 2.33E-18 kg at the tip) is smaller
$ than the machine precision (~2.2E-16). The old filter compared each term with
$ EPSIL(1), deleted the whole mass matrix and stopped with error 9776 (NEV<1).
$
$ Silicon-like beam: L = 1 um, b = 0.2 um, t = 0.1 um
$   E = 1.7E11 Pa, nu = 0.28, rho = 2330 kg/m^3
$   A  = 2.0E-14 m^2
$   I1 = b*t^3/12 = 1.66667E-29 m^4 (bending in plane 1, deflection in Y)
$   I2 = t*b^3/12 = 6.66667E-29 m^4 (bending in plane 2, deflection in Z)
$   J  = 0.2287*b*t^3 = 4.574E-29 m^4
$ All stiffness terms are much larger than 2.2E-16, so the absolute stiffness
$ filter and AUTOSPC are not involved: this deck tests mass only.
$
$ Expected results (CBAR mass is lumped, translational only):
$   Total mass (GPWG) = rho*A*L = 4.66E-17 kg
$   Mode  10-element FE (Hz)   Euler-Bernoulli continuum (Hz)
$     1      1.37353E+08          1.37983E+08    1st bending, Y
$     2      2.74706E+08          2.75967E+08    1st bending, Z
$     3      8.51199E+08          8.64727E+08    2nd bending, Y
$ The FE column is the exact eigensolution of this mesh, so MYSTRAN should
$ match it to about 5 significant figures.
$
ECHO          = UNSORT
METHOD        = 1
DISP          = ALL
BEGIN BULK
$
EIGRL          1                       3       0                    MASS
$
GRID           1              0.      0.      0.          123456
GRID           2           1.e-7      0.      0.
GRID           3           2.e-7      0.      0.
GRID           4           3.e-7      0.      0.
GRID           5           4.e-7      0.      0.
GRID           6           5.e-7      0.      0.
GRID           7           6.e-7      0.      0.
GRID           8           7.e-7      0.      0.
GRID           9           8.e-7      0.      0.
GRID          10           9.e-7      0.      0.
GRID          11           1.e-6      0.      0.
$
CBAR           1       1       1       2      0.      1.      0.
CBAR           2       1       2       3      0.      1.      0.
CBAR           3       1       3       4      0.      1.      0.
CBAR           4       1       4       5      0.      1.      0.
CBAR           5       1       5       6      0.      1.      0.
CBAR           6       1       6       7      0.      1.      0.
CBAR           7       1       7       8      0.      1.      0.
CBAR           8       1       8       9      0.      1.      0.
CBAR           9       1       9      10      0.      1.      0.
CBAR          10       1      10      11      0.      1.      0.
$
$       PID             MID             A               I1
PBAR*                  1               1         2.0E-14  1.66666667E-29*
$       I2              J
*         6.66666667E-29       4.574E-29
$
MAT1           1  1.7+11             .28   2330.
$
PARAM   GRDPNT   0
PARAM   POST     -1
$
ENDDATA
